// The parts of a path as text (`std/builtin/os.taut`): `path_parent` and
// `path_name` answer as `dirname` and `basename` do, and `path_join` puts a
// name under a folder. They touch no file, so they need no permission.

@ cases.a-path-is-taken-apart-as-dirname-and-basename-do
source = ```nib
import std::builtin::os { path_join, path_name, path_parent }
show(&path_parent("/a/b/c"))
show(&path_parent("/a/b/"))
show(&path_parent("/a"))
show(&path_parent("/"))
show(&path_parent("x"))
show(&path_parent("x/y"))
show(&path_name("/a/b/c"))
show(&path_name("/a/b/"))
show(&path_name("/"))
show(&path_join("/a", "b"))
show(&path_join("/a/", "b"))
show(&path_join("/a", "/b"))
```
stdout = ```
"/a/b"
"/a"
"/"
"/"
"."
"x"
"c"
"b"
"/"
"/a/b"
"/a/b"
"/b"
```
